==Trivia==
*Ultimate Wildmutt is the last [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate form]] used by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
**He was included in the script outline for an early version of the second episode for '''Omniverse''', ''[[Tangled Web: Part 2]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/9/92/Tangled_Web_P2_Script_Outline.pdf/revision/latest ''Tangled Web: Part 2'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
**The '''Omniverse''' crew did not discuss bringing Ultimate Wildmutt back as one of [[Albedo]]'s transformations.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = FreelanceArt}}
*Ultimate Wildmutt's sentient counterpart did not appear in ''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]'', even though the synopsis said that ''all'' of the [[Ultimate Forms#Sentient Forms|Sentient Ultimate Forms]] want freedom.
*Ultimate Wildmutt was first revealed on the DVD cover of ''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Wild Truth]]''.
*Ultimate Wildmutt was originally intended to be the size of a chihuahua and was incapable of speaking human languages.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/7/79/Prisoner_775_is_Missing_Draft-1.pdf ''Prisoner 775 is Missing'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] did concept art for Ultimate Wildmutt as part of freelance work, who used inspiration from looking at dinosaurs. However, none of his designs were used for the final version.{{Refn|https://archive.is/V7jBL|group = DJW|name = FreelanceArt}}{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Ultimate Wildmutt.png]]|group = DJW}}
**One of Ultimate Wildmutt's unused concept art by Jon Suzuki would later be repurposed as the basis for [[Solid Plugg]]'s design.{{Refn|[[:File:Solid Plugg Originally Ultimate Wildmutt.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

